 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# `indic/05` — Information Parity (IP)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose:** Compute Information Parity (IP) — a measure of how much more a\n",
    "language model struggles to compress Indic-script text compared to English.\n",
    "IP captures the **semantic density** dimension of encoder burden, complementing\n",
    "the surface-level fragmentation captured by TP (computed in `indic/04`).\n",
    "\n",
    "IP is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\text{IP}(L) = \\frac{\\text{NLL}(w_E)}{\\text{NLL}(w_L)}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where NLL is the **total** (summed) negative log-likelihood under BLOOM-560M\n",
    "using a causal language modelling objective. A value of 1.0 means the model\n",
    "compresses the Indic language as well as English; values well below 1.0\n",
    "indicate the model finds the language harder to predict.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why total NLL, not mean NLL?** Using the sum keeps TP and IP conceptually\n",
    "independent. Mean NLL conflates IP with TP: an Indic sentence produces more\n",
    "tokens per word, so its mean per-token NLL would appear artificially lower\n",
    "even if each token were equally hard.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prerequisite:** Run `indic/04` first — this notebook reads the same\n",
    "`data/indic/<ISO>_indicmt.csv` files and expects `src_tc` to already exist.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reads:** `data/indic/<ISO>_indicmt.csv`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Outputs:** Adds columns `ip_nat` and `ip_rom` to each per-language CSV.\n",
    "\n",
    "**IP interpretation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| IP value | Interpretation |\n",
    "|----------|----------------|\n",
    "| 1.0 | Model compresses Indic as well as English — perfectly fair |\n",
    "| 0.7 | Model finds Indic 30% harder than English |\n",
    "| 0.5 | Model finds Indic much harder than English — high bias |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "**References**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Tsvetkov, A. & Kipnis, A. (2024). Information parity: Measuring and predicting\n",
    "  the multilingual capabilities of language models. *EMNLP 2024 Findings*,\n",
    "  pp. 7971–7989.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Kanjirangat, V., Samardžić, T., Dolamic, L., & Rinaldi, F. (2025).\n",
    "  Tokenization and representation biases in multilingual models on dialectal\n",
    "  NLP tasks. *EMNLP 2025*, pp. 23992–24010.\n",
    "  https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.20045\n",
    "\n",
    "- BigScience Workshop. (2022). BLOOM: A 176B-Parameter Open-Access\n",
    "  Multilingual Language Model. https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.05100\n",
    "\n",
    "- Conneau, A., et al. (2020). Unsupervised cross-lingual representation\n",
    "  learning at scale. *ACL 2020*, pp. 8440–8451.\n",
    "  https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.02116\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sai B., A., et al. (2023). IndicMT Eval: A Dataset to Meta-Evaluate Machine\n",
    "  Translation Metrics for Indian Languages. *ACL 2023*, pp. 14210–14228.\n",
    "  https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.795"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "install_deps",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import subprocess, sys\n",
    "\n",
    "def _install(pkg):\n",
    "    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', pkg, '-q'])\n",
    "\n",
    "for pkg in ['torch', 'transformers', 'accelerate', 'pandas']:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        __import__(pkg)\n",
    "    except ImportError:\n",
    "        print(f'Installing {pkg}...'); _install(pkg)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dependencies ready.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_config",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "All paths are relative to the repository root.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `BATCH_SIZE` — sentences per forward pass through BLOOM. Reduce to 4 on CPU\n",
    "  if you run out of memory.\n",
    "- `MAX_LENGTH` — truncation limit for the BLOOM tokenizer. Set to 256 to\n",
    "  reduce truncation on longer Indic sentences while keeping memory manageable.\n",
    "- `DEVICE` — set to `\"cuda\"` if a GPU is available. BLOOM-560M is usable on\n",
    "  CPU but will be slow (~2–4 hours for 7,000 × 2 conditions)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "config",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path('data/indic')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Column names ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "SRC_COL     = 'src'\n",
    "HYP_COL     = 'hyp'\n",
    "HYP_ROM_COL = 'hyp_rom'\n",
    "REF_COL     = 'ref'\n",
    "REF_ROM_COL = 'ref_rom'\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Language config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "LANGUAGES = ['GUJ', 'HIN', 'MAL', 'MAR', 'TAM']\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Model / inference config ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "MODEL_NAME = 'bigscience/bloom-560m'\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 8       # reduce to 4 on low-memory CPU\n",
    "MAX_LENGTH = 256     # raised from 128 to reduce truncation on Indic\n",
    "DEVICE     = 'cpu'   # change to 'cuda' if a GPU is available\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Data directory : {DATA_DIR.resolve()}')\n",
    "print(f'Model          : {MODEL_NAME}')\n",
    "print(f'Device         : {DEVICE}')\n",
    "print(f'Batch size     : {BATCH_SIZE}')\n",
    "print(f'Max length     : {MAX_LENGTH}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_model",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Load BLOOM-560M\n",
    "\n",
    "BLOOM-560M is a multilingual decoder-only language model used here as a\n",
    "compression proxy. Its NLL over a sentence measures how predictable the\n",
    "model finds that text — lower NLL means the model understands the language\n",
    "better.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Padding side:** BLOOM defaults to left-padding, which corrupts position\n",
    "embeddings in batched inference and inflates NLL for non-zero-position\n",
    "sentences. We override with right-padding so all real tokens start at\n",
    "position 0.\n",
    "\n",
    "The first run will download model weights (~1.1 GB). Subsequent runs use\n",
    "the Hugging Face cache."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "load_model",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loading tokenizer: {MODEL_NAME}')\n",
    "bloom_tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME)\n",
    "bloom_tokenizer.padding_side = 'right'  # override left-pad default\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Loading model: {MODEL_NAME}')\n",
    "print('(First run downloads ~1.1 GB — one-time)')\n",
    "bloom_model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME, torch_dtype=torch.float32)\n",
    "bloom_model = bloom_model.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "bloom_model.eval()\n",
    "print('Model ready.\\n')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_nll",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — NLL Helper Function\n",
    "\n",
    "The `compute_nll` function returns the **total** (summed) cross-entropy loss\n",
    "for each input string using the causal language modelling objective.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key design choices:\n",
    "- **Total NLL, not mean.** Using the sum keeps IP and TP independent.\n",
    "  Mean NLL would conflate IP with TP (longer token sequences appear\n",
    "  easier when NLL is averaged, which is an artefact of tokenization,\n",
    "  not of semantic understanding).\n",
    "- **Right-padding + attention mask.** Pad tokens are excluded from the\n",
    "  loss sum via the attention mask, so they never contribute to NLL.\n",
    "- **NaN guards.** Zero NLL is degenerate (perfect prediction), so any\n",
    "  zero value is replaced with NaN before computing the ratio."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "nll_fn",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def compute_nll(texts: list, batch_size: int = BATCH_SIZE) -> list:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Return per-sentence total NLL for each string in `texts`.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Uses total cross-entropy (sum over real tokens, not mean), so that\n",
    "    IP and TP remain conceptually independent.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for i in range(0, len(texts), batch_size):\n",
    "        batch_raw = texts[i : i + batch_size]\n",
    "\n",
    "        valid_indices, valid_texts = [], []\n",
    "        for j, text in enumerate(batch_raw):\n",
    "            if text and not (isinstance(text, float) and pd.isna(text)):\n",
    "                valid_indices.append(j)\n",
    "                valid_texts.append(str(text))\n",
    "\n",
    "        batch_results = [float('nan')] * len(batch_raw)\n",
    "        if not valid_texts:\n",
    "            results.extend(batch_results)\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "\n",
    "        enc = bloom_tokenizer(\n",
    "            valid_texts,\n",
    "            return_tensors='pt',\n",
    "            padding=True,\n",
    "            truncation=True,\n",
    "            max_length=MAX_LENGTH,\n",
    "        ).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            logits = bloom_model(**enc).logits\n",
    "\n",
    "        for k, orig_idx in enumerate(valid_indices):\n",
    "            input_ids  = enc['input_ids'][k]\n",
    "            attn_mask  = enc['attention_mask'][k]\n",
    "\n",
    "            # causal LM: position t predicts t+1, shift by one\n",
    "            shift_logits = logits[k, :-1, :]\n",
    "            shift_labels = input_ids[1:]\n",
    "            shift_mask   = attn_mask[1:].bool()\n",
    "\n",
    "            if shift_mask.sum() == 0:\n",
    "                batch_results[orig_idx] = float('nan')\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "\n",
    "            total_nll = F.cross_entropy(\n",
    "                shift_logits[shift_mask],\n",
    "                shift_labels[shift_mask],\n",
    "                reduction='sum',\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            batch_results[orig_idx] = total_nll.item()\n",
    "\n",
    "        results.extend(batch_results)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_load",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Load Per-Language CSVs\n",
    "\n",
    "Read the CSVs updated by `indic/04`. Checks that `src`, `hyp`, `ref`,\n",
    "`hyp_rom`, and `ref_rom` are all present."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "load_csvs",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "data = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "REQUIRED = [SRC_COL, HYP_COL, REF_COL, HYP_ROM_COL, REF_ROM_COL]\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso in LANGUAGES:\n",
    "    path = DATA_DIR / f'{iso}_indicmt.csv'\n",
    "    if not path.exists():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "            f'{path} not found. Run indic/01, indic/02, and indic/04 first.')\n",
    "    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n",
    "    data[iso] = df\n",
    "\n",
    "    present = [c for c in REQUIRED if c in df.columns]\n",
    "    missing = [c for c in REQUIRED if c not in df.columns]\n",
    "    status  = 'OK' if not missing else f'MISSING: {missing}'\n",
    "    print(f'  {iso}  {len(df):,} rows  |  required cols: {status}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nLoaded {len(data)} language files.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_compute_ip",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Compute IP Across All Five Languages\n",
    "\n",
    "For each language file we:\n",
    "1. Compute total NLL for the English source (denominator, shared across\n",
    "   all four IP columns per language)\n",
    "2. Compute total NLL for each Indic column (numerator)\n",
    "3. Divide: $\\text{IP} = \\text{NLL}(w_E) / \\text{NLL}(w_L)$\n",
    "4. Save a checkpoint CSV after each language\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell is safe to re-run — it checks whether the IP column already\n",
    "exists before inserting, so partial results are preserved.\n",
    "\n",
    "IP columns added: `ip_nat` (hypothesis, native script), `ip_ref`\n",
    "(reference, native script), `ip_rom` (hypothesis, romanised),\n",
    "`ip_ref_rom` (reference, romanised)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "compute_ip",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# (ip_output_col, text_col)\n",
    "IP_PAIRS = [\n",
    "    ('ip_nat',     HYP_COL),\n",
    "    ('ip_ref',     REF_COL),\n",
    "    ('ip_rom',     HYP_ROM_COL),\n",
    "    ('ip_ref_rom', REF_ROM_COL),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"{'='*55}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{iso} — Information Parity\")\n",
    "    print(f\"{'='*55}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # English NLL (denominator) — compute once per language\n",
    "    print('  Computing English NLL (denominator)...')\n",
    "    nll_eng = (\n",
    "        pd.Series(compute_nll(df[SRC_COL].fillna('').tolist()))\n",
    "          .replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    if 'src_nll' not in df.columns:\n",
    "        df.insert(df.columns.get_loc(SRC_COL) + 1, 'src_nll', nll_eng.values)\n",
    "\n",
    "    for ip_col, text_col in IP_PAIRS:\n",
    "        if text_col not in df.columns:\n",
    "            print(f\"  '{text_col}' not found — skipped\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        if ip_col in df.columns:\n",
    "            print(f\"  '{ip_col}' already present — skipped\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "\n",
    "        print(f\"  Computing NLL for {text_col}...\")\n",
    "        nll_indic = (\n",
    "            pd.Series(compute_nll(df[text_col].fillna('').tolist()))\n",
    "              .replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        ip_series = nll_eng / nll_indic\n",
    "        df.insert(df.columns.get_loc(text_col) + 1, ip_col, ip_series.values)\n",
    "        mean_ip = ip_series.mean()\n",
    "        print(f\"  {ip_col:<14}  mean IP = {mean_ip:.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Checkpoint save after each language\n",
    "    out_path = DATA_DIR / f'{iso}_indicmt.csv'\n",
    "    df.to_csv(out_path, index=False)\n",
    "    print(f\"  [checkpoint] {out_path}\")\n",
    "    data[iso] = df\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_ip_inv",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — TP–IP Inversion Check\n",
    "\n",
    "Under romanisation, IP is expected to **collapse** for every Indic language\n",
    "(Latin-script Indic digrams are not in BLOOM's training distribution, so\n",
    "the model finds romanised Indic text much harder to predict).\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the TP–IP Inversion: TP inflates (more tokens) while IP collapses\n",
    "(less meaning per token) simultaneously — the worst possible combination\n",
    "for a similarity-based evaluation metric.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cell computes $\\Delta\\text{IP} = \\text{ip\_rom} - \\text{ip\_nat}$ and\n",
    "confirms the direction is negative for all five languages."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "ip_inversion",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "print(f\"{'Lang':6s}  {'IP_nat':>8s}  {'IP_rom':>8s}  {'Delta_IP':>10s}  {'Delta%':>8s}\")\n",
    "print('-' * 52)\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    if 'ip_nat' not in df.columns or 'ip_rom' not in df.columns:\n",
    "        print(f'  {iso}  — ip_nat or ip_rom missing, skipped')\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "\n",
    "    ip_nat = df['ip_nat'].mean()\n",
    "    ip_rom = df['ip_rom'].mean()\n",
    "    delta  = ip_rom - ip_nat\n",
    "    pct    = (delta / ip_nat) * 100\n",
    "    arrow  = '↓' if delta < 0 else '↑'\n",
    "    print(f'  {iso:4s}  {ip_nat:>8.3f}  {ip_rom:>8.3f}  {arrow}{delta:>9.3f}  {pct:>+7.1f}%')\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Expected: Delta_IP < 0 (IP collapses) for all five languages under romanisation.')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('Combined with TP inflation from indic/04, this is the TP-IP Inversion:')\n",
    "print('  romanisation produces MORE tokens that each carry LESS meaning.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md_tpip_table",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Joint TP–IP Summary Table\n",
    "\n",
    "Print native-script TP and IP side-by-side for all five languages.\n",
    "These values feed directly into the SBI and IPI diagnostics computed\n",
    "in `indic/06`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "joint_summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "print(f\"{'Lang':6s}  {'TP_nat':>8s}  {'TP_rom':>8s}  {'IP_nat':>8s}  {'IP_rom':>8s}\")\n",
    "print('-' * 55)\n",
    "\n",
    "for iso, df in data.items():\n",
    "    def _m(col):\n",
    "        return f\"{df[col].mean():.3f}\" if col in df.columns else '--'\n",
    "    print(f\"  {iso:4s}  {_m('tp_nat'):>8s}  {_m('tp_rom'):>8s}  \"",
    "          f\"{_m('ip_nat'):>8s}  {_m('ip_rom'):>8s}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('TP > 1.0 : encoder over-fragments relative to English')\n",
    "print('IP < 1.0 : encoder finds the language harder to compress than English')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print('data/indic/ is ready for indic/06 (SBI, IPI, and Computational Tax).')"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
